-- title:
--   Trivial inertia at the Gauss valuation of K₁/K₂
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_1$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange` of `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p`, i.e. the field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_f)/\mathrm{intSeriesC}(p_g)$ of integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms of the same weight for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$ (with nonzero denominator), and let $K_2$ be the corresponding field built from $\Gamma_0(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as fraction field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with $K_1$ an $A$-algebra compatibly over $L$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_1$ consisting exactly of those $f$ for which there exist $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ (the Gauss valuation ring). Let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $K_1$ by ring automorphisms, fixing every element of $K_1$ that lies in $K_2$ and with every $G$-invariant element of $K_1$ lying in $K_2$. Then every $g \in G$ such that $g \cdot f - f$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ for all $f \in W_0$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the triviality of the inertia group of the Gauss valuation inside the Galois group $G$ of $K_1/K_2$: an automorphism inducing the identity on the residue field of $W_0$, the function field of the good component of the special fibre, is the identity. It is used in the identification of inertia at supersingular points of $X_0(Mp)$ with stabilisers of level structures, where two diamond operators agreeing on the special fibre must coincide.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneGammaZeroP_eq_one_of_forall_smul_sub_mem_nonunits_gauss_x1x0_gamma0.lean

